        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Me 262 Project\n- Places: Paine Field, Everett, Washington, United States, Seattle\n- Products: Messerschmitt Me 262\n- Concepts: Aircraft nicknames, jet-powered fighter aircraft\n\nFacts:\n- The Me 262 Project is based at Paine Field in Everett, Washington, United States, near Seattle.\n- The Messerschmitt Me 262 was the world's first operational jet-powered fighter aircraft.\n- The Messerschmitt Me 262 was nicknamed Schwalbe in fighter versions.\n- The Messerschmitt Me 262 was nicknamed Sturmvogel in fighter-bomber versions.",
